y that has just recently completely  Fallen apart even as a representation  but that's how we talk  modern astronomy has led to some  wonderful things  satellites for instance for smartphones  on which you can listen to the Michael  Knowles show phones on which you can go  to the bookstore and you can order my  books speechless controlling words  controlling Minds reasons to vote for  Democrats make superb Christmas presents  the wonderful things about astronomy  astronomy has also created a new  representation that makes man appear  random and insignificant and the  Scientific Revolution as a whole which  has helped to build our modern world has  placed in our Collective imagination a  representation of reality is  fundamentally physical  many of the greatest scientists in  history have been religious at least two  of the men that I just mentioned Mendel  and lemetra were Catholic priests and  Copernicus maybe was too he was at the  very least a Catholic Canon if not a  priest uh so I'm not casting aspersions  on scientists other than Dr fauci I am  casting many aspersions on Dr bouchi but  but on the other scientists I'm really  not  but our modern conception of reality is  fundamentally physical  is not the result of some nefarious  scientist it is a feature not a bug of  the whole Scientific Revolution which  necessarily considers the world only as  physical  the philosopher Owen Barfield predicted  all of this half a century ago in his  book saving the appearances Barfield saw  that the scientific worldview left  unchecked would eventually eliminate all  meaning and all coherence from the  cosmos he saw that it would lose its  grip on any principle of unity pervading  nature as a whole and the knowledge of  nature that it would give rise to the  hypothesis of chance Randomness creeping  from the theory of evolution into the  theory of the physical foundation of the  Earth itself and still worse cause an  increasing fragmentation of science  quote pigeonholed kn